pseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":175,"output":78,"cacheRead":1792,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":2045,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793949074287,"responseId":"d3e20b42-2aaf-410c-861c-0e82394d331d"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_fxqSc84fEZYRjh1SJ2sy3294","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"=== note.txt ===\nmarket-test\n\n=== seed.txt ===\nalpha 100\nbeta 200\ngamma 300\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1793949076348},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The directory is basically empty with some test files. Now I need to write a short market note about ethanol stocks to notes.md.\n\nLet me write a concise market note about ethanol stocks.","thinkingSignature":"5a0cc3dc-fabe-41ed-824a-c245be1e4544"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_AB7w0DVKYr1GLLcxZTnj2134","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"/tmp/work/notes.md","content":"# Market Note: Ethanol Stocks\n\n*Date: 2026-11-06*\n\n## Overview\n\nEthanol producers remain a mixed bag heading into the winter months. The\nsector is tightly linked to corn prices, crude oil, and the Renewable Fuel\nStandard (RFS), so a few key variables are worth watching.\n\n## Key Drivers\n\n- **Corn input costs** — Feedstock is the single largest cost line. Lower corn\n  futures generally expand crush margins for producers.\n- **Crude / gasoline** — Ethanol prices track the energy complex; a firmer\n  crude bid lifts blending economics.\n- **RFS / policy** — Renewable volume obligations and any change to blending\n  mandates (E15 year-round, small-refinery exemptions) move the group.\n- **Exports** — Brazil and China demand can swing quarterly results.\n\n## Notable Names\n\n| Ticker | Company | Note |\n|--------|---------|------|\n| ADM | Archer-Daniels-Midland | Diversified; ethanol is one leg of a broader agribusiness |\n| GPP | Green Plains Partners | Pure-play producer; high operating leverage to margins |\n| VLO | Valero | Refiner with meaningful ethanol exposure via subsidiaries |\n| REX | REX American Resources | Smaller pure-play; volatile but levered to the theme |\n\n## Takeaway\n\nThe group is a margin story first and a volume story second. Watch the\ncorn-to-ethanol spread; when it widens, the pure-plays tend to outperform.\nPolicy headlines can create sharp, short-lived moves, so size positions\naccordingly.\n"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":162,"output":432,"cacheRead":1920,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":2514,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793949076348,"responseId":"5a0cc3dc-fabe-41ed-824a-c245be1e4544"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_AB7w0DVKYr1GLLcxZTnj2134","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Blocked: \"/tmp/work/notes.md\" resolves outside the workspace (/workspace). Journalist drafts and charts belong under the workspace only."}],"details":{},"isError":true,"timestamp":1793949088957},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Interesting - the write tool is blocked because it says the path resolves outside the workspace (/workspace). But the current working directory is /tmp/work. There seems to be a mismatch. Let me check what the workspace actually is.","thinkingSignature":"16f9d357-c18f-45a2-9458-551b85014d7d"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_wVshVQ416i1FOUbffqHY0466","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"pwd; echo \"---\"; ls -la /workspace 2>&1; echo \"---\"; ls -la /tmp/work"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":122,"output":116,"cacheRead":2432,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":2670,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793949088958,"responseId":"16f9d357-c18f-45a2-9458-551b85014d7d"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_wVshVQ416i1FOUbffqHY0466","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"/tmp/work\n---\ntotal 16\ndrwx------ 4 hg   hg   4096 Nov  6 06:57 .\ndrwxr-xr-x 1 root root 4096 Nov  6 06:28 ..\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 hg   hg   4096 Nov  6 07:10 journalist-pi\ndrwxr-xr-x 4 hg   hg   4096 Nov  6 07:10 pi\n---\ntotal 1\ndrwxr-xr-x  2 hg   hg    80 Nov  6 06:36 .\ndrwxrwxrwt 12 root root 900 Nov  6 07:11 ..\n-rw-r--r--  1 hg   hg    12 Nov  6 06:36 note.txt\n-rw-r--r--  1 hg   hg    29 Nov  6 06:36 seed.txt\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1793949091669},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The workspace is /workspace. The write tool blocks writing outside /workspace. So I need to write notes.md under /workspace. Let me check what's in /workspace and write there.\n\nThe current working directory is /tmp/work, but the write tool restricts to /workspace. Let me write to /workspace/notes.md.","thinkingSignature":"9d77cab2-cead-4efd-ba54-9c366490b409"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_00_gzJdvcaXUXTpDpaQLBac0470","name":"write","arguments":{"content":"# Market Note: Ethanol Stocks\n\n*Date: 2026-11-06*\n\n## Overview\n\nEthanol producers remain a mixed bag heading into the winter months. The\nsector is tightly linked to corn prices, crude oil, and the Renewable Fuel\nStandard (RFS), so a few key variables are worth watching.\n\n## Key Drivers\n\n- **Corn input costs** — Feedstock is the single largest cost line. Lower corn\n  futures generally expand crush margins for producers.\n- **Crude / gasoline** — Ethanol prices track the energy complex; a firmer\n  crude bid lifts blending economics.\n- **RFS / policy** — Renewable volume obligations and any change to blending\n  mandates (E15 year-round, small-refinery exemptions) move the group.\n- **Exports** — Brazil and China demand can swing quarterly results.\n\n## Notable Names\n\n| Ticker | Company | Note |\n|--------|---------|------|\n| ADM | Archer-Daniels-Midland | Diversified; ethanol is one leg of a broader agribusiness |\n| GPP | Green Plains Partners | Pure-play producer; high operating leverage to margins |\n| VLO | Valero | Refiner with meaningful ethanol exposure via subsidiaries |\n| REX | REX American Resources | Smaller pure-play; volatile but levered to the theme |\n\n## Takeaway\n\nThe group is a margin story first and a volume story second. Watch the\ncorn-to-ethanol spread; when it widens, the pure-plays tend to outperform.\nPolicy headlines can create sharp, short-lived moves, so size positions\naccordingly.\n","path":"/workspace/notes.md"}}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"deepseek-v4-pro","usage":{"input":322,"output":467,"cacheRead":2560,"cacheWrite":0,"totalTokens":3349,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1793949091669,"responseId":"9d77cab2-cead-4efd-ba54-9c366490b409"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_00_gzJdvcaXUXTpDpaQLBac0470","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote 1420 bytes to /workspace/notes.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1793949098076},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","thinkingSignature":"b2634da5-e0ea-4d7c-88ab-577f5d33b120"},{"type":"text","text":"Done. Here's a quick summary of what I found and did:\n\n**Directory exploration** (`/tmp/work`):\n- `note.txt` → contains `market-test`\n- `seed.txt` → `alpha 100`, `beta 200`, `gamma 300`\n- Otherwise empty.\n\n**Note:** The write tool restricts file writes to `/workspace`, so I saved the note there instead of `/tmp/work`.\n\nI wrote a short market note on **ethanol stocks** to `/workspace/notes.md`, covering:\n- **Key drivers** — corn input costs, crude/gasoline, RFS policy, and exports\n- **Notable names** — ADM, GPP, VLO, and REX with one-line rationales\n- **Takeaway** — it's a margin story first; watch the corn-to-ethanol spread and size positions for policy-driven volatility."}],"api":"anthropic-messages","provider":"anthropic","model":"deepse